&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer on the Professional Services team, you’ll work hands-on-keyboard inside strategic enterprise customers, modernizing legacy frontends to Next.js and building production AI agents. You’ll own the work from technical discovery to shipped TypeScript, whether that’s moving a React app to App Router, auditing a codebase for performance, or deploying agents with Vercel’s eve framework and AI SDK. The role has two profiles: Next.js experts focus on code optimization, performance audits, and SEO and AEO (answer engine optimization), while AI builders scope, design, and ship agents that prove their value. This is a hybrid role with 3 in-office days per week in San Francisco, New York City, or Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build production AI agents, MCP servers, and agentic workflows with Vercel’s eve framework, AI SDK, and AI Cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead migrations from legacy React, Vue, and other frameworks to Next.js, including Pages Router to App Router, and automate them where possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit customer codebases for performance bottlenecks and anti-patterns, and deliver roadmaps with measurable improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect Next.js applications with App Router, Server Components, streaming, and ISR for enterprise scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run workshops and pair programming so customer teams can maintain what you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software engineering experience, including 2+ years in a customer-facing technical role (consulting, solutions architecture, forward deployed engineering, or technical founder)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built and deployed web applications, backend systems, or agentic workflows using AI tooling such as harnesses, skills, and MCP servers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level TypeScript and React experience shipping production applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Next.js experts: Led a legacy frontend migration to Next.js, or shipped a production Next.js application using App Router and Server Components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI builders: Built production LLM agents, including sandbox and filesystem agent patterns and human-in-the-loop flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ran technical discovery and presented to executives at enterprise customers, with occasional travel to customer sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led an enterprise AI initiative that shipped production agents replacing manual processes or legacy systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnosed and fixed LCP, CLS, and INP issues at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributed to Next.js, React, or AI SDK open source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $137,000.00 - $207,000.00.&amp;nbsp; This salary range is an estimate. Actual salary will be based on job related skills, experience and location. Pay ranges outside San Francisco may be&amp;nbsp; adjusted based on employee location.&amp;nbsp; The total compensation package also includes benefits and equity-based compensation. Your recruiter can share more about the specific pay range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
